# Deepway Navigator: "When this creature enters, untap each other Merfolk you control." Bot1's Coral Merfolk attacked on turn 3 and
# is still tapped on Bot2's turn 4, when Bot2's own Coral Merfolk attacks too. After combat Bot1 flashes the Navigator in: its
# trigger untaps Bot1's Merfolk, and Bot2's tapped Merfolk - not one Bot1 controls - stays tapped.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Coral Merfolk
Mox Pearl
Deepway Navigator
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Coral Merfolk
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Coral Merfolk.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Coral Merfolk.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Attack(Coral Merfolk > Bot2)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Coral Merfolk.Tapped = true
Bot2.Attack(Coral Merfolk > Bot1)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Deepway Navigator.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Coral Merfolk.Tapped = false
Bot2.Battlefield.Coral Merfolk.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Deepway Navigator.Tapped = false
